CODE FUZZY MATCH
Codes are alphanumeric combinations. Common patterns:
Letters+digits: HE3363, MB6501, MG38F
Letter+digits+letters alternating: B52A003A, M0861SU
2L+digits+2L: BD265MO, CE02RR, F10SR
Prefix+digits: HP2022JN, Wk-801, SC201LV
Short codes: B57, S65, 118N, SG5
Dash codes: P2H-AT, KL-31, TK-700

When user speaks a code:
1. Reconstruct from spoken input ("H E thirty three sixty three" → HE3363)
2. Read back character by character to confirm
3. If two possible matches → offer both ("HE3363 or HE3364?")
4. After 2 failed attempts → "I'll note it down, our team will confirm the grade."

